  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the most favorable outcome with the minimum probability—here, 0 Euros in Lottery B with 20% probability—while Lottery A has no such low-probability favorable outcome. The individual considers exactly this possibility: 'maybe I will be lucky and lose nothing,' which directly references the 0 Euro outcome in Lottery B. The comparison of information and the weight given to the possibility of avoiding loss aligns with attention to the least probable but most favorable outcome. The individual’s justification mirrors the logic of the decision reason by giving decision weight to the best outcome that occurs with the lowest probability (in B), even if it's not certain. Therefore, both the information considered and the justification match the structure of the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
